{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-05 governs this trip, and the rider's 21.0 km arithmetic is run against the wrong itinerary. Both endpoints were amended after booking: the rider moved the pin to Punggol MRT PHV pickup bay at 07:12:30 (trip_record.pickup_amended_at) and, mid-journey, changed the destination to Changi Terminal 3 at 07:41:52 (trip_record.dropoff_amended_at). POL-RD-05 expressly covers a rider moving the pin, a rider giving a different address in the chat_log and a terminal change from T1 to T3, and it directs that POL-RD-01 be re-applied against the optimal route between the AMENDED endpoints. That route is a stored field on the trip record — amended_optimal_distance_km 24.60 with amended_optimal_duration_min 31.0 — and the tribunal must read it rather than re-derive it. The 21.0 km figure is the optimum between Blk 118 Rivervale Drive and Terminal 1, an itinerary that was never driven.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-CHAT-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.amended_optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the governing amended baseline the excess falls below the POL-RD-01 gate and no deviation exists. The trace measures 26.17 km — and POL-RD-01 says that where trace_distance_km and the rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km (26.2) disagree, the trace governs — against an amended optimal of 24.60 km. That is an excess of 1.57 km, 6.4% of the optimal distance. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is BOTH greater than 20% of optimal_distance_km AND greater than 0.8 km; the percentage limb fails by a wide margin (6.4% against 20%), and both tests must pass. POL-RD-01 then says in terms that if either establishment test fails, no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip, the only exception being a billing-integrity refund under POL-RD-09(4), which does not arise on this fare breakdown.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The platform's default deviation block reports excess_km 5.17 and excess_pct 24.62 only because it measures the driven trace against the superseded booked optimum of 21.0 km. POL-RD-05 forbids exactly that substitution and adds that distance driven before an amendment timestamp is never counted as excess against the driver. The booked optimum predates both amendment timestamps recorded on the trip record, and the extra distance the rider now objects to is the Punggol-to-Terminal-3 leg that she herself asked for. Once POL-RD-01 is re-run on the amended route, the threshold test fails and the rider's 'this trip is usually 21 km' comparison drops out of the case.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-CHAT-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and has not discharged it. The trace she would have to rely on is unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 206 fixes at a 10 second sample interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0, and no POL-RD-07(a)-(c) defect — so the trace is admissible and clean, but what it shows on the amended baseline is an excess of 1.57 km, i.e. 6.4%, which does not meet the POL-RD-01 threshold limb (b) requires her to prove. Her profile does not rescue the claim either: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1, far below the 4-or-more that POL-RD-08's enhanced-corroboration test requires, so no additional corroboration is called for and none is offered.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-RPROF-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's complaint that the driver 'drove around the airport for another five minutes' does not carry the claim, even taken at its highest. POL-RD-05 excludes from excess the distance driven around an amended dropoff point where the rider was not at it and the trace shows the vehicle circling within 400 m; and the excess on the amended baseline is already only 1.57 km, below the POL-RD-01 gate, before any such exclusion is applied. Whatever happened on the Terminal 3 kerb approach, it cannot convert a 6.4% variance into a refundable deviation, because the threshold is a single numeric gate that ordinary manoeuvring does not open.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-CHAT-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no repeat-deviation pattern to weigh against the driver. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 across driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 402, so neither limb of the POL-RD-06 test is met — not 3 or more flags, and not the 0.05 ratio (which would require 21 flags) with the 40-trip floor satisfied. POL-RD-06 is in any event not engaged on this trip, because no MATERIAL deviation (greater than 50% or greater than 8.0 km of excess) is recorded once the amended baseline is used. Only the two profile fields POL-RD-06 names have been cited here, as POL-GEN-01 requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-GPS-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The pass-through layer produces nothing for the rider either. The fare breakdown carries tolls_erp 0.00 with an empty erp_gantries list, waiting_time_fee 0.00, and airport_surcharge 0.00 — correctly so, because this trip ENDS at Changi rather than originating there, and no surcharge is chargeable or charged. There is therefore no phantom gantry and no wrongly applied surcharge for POL-RD-09(4) to correct as a standalone billing-integrity refund, and no off-route ERP to be itemised or added on top of anything. The charging lines on this trip all have counterparts in the trace and trip record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory covers this trip: EV-ADVIS-00108-01 is MISSING, carries weight_multiplier 0.0 and the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, which is disclosed here as POL-GEN-02(1) requires. That absence decides nothing in this case, because the driver has never asserted an external traffic cause that would need an advisory to be tested under POL-RD-03 or discarded under POL-RD-13. His explanation is the rider's own two endpoint amendments in the chat log — 'ok noted' at 07:12:15 and 'ok changing now' at 07:42:05 — and it is supported on the record by the stored amended-optimal figures, not by any assertion about conditions on the road.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00108-01", "EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-CHAT-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-05", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both of you: this trip must be judged against the route that was actually ordered. It was booked from Blk 118 Rivervale Drive to Changi Terminal 1, but the rider moved the pickup to Punggol MRT PHV pickup bay at 07:12:30 and then, mid-journey, asked for the destination to be changed to Terminal 3 at 07:41:52. Both are recorded in the app chat (EV-CHAT-00108) and on the trip record (EV-TRIP-00108). POL-RD-05 governs exactly this situation: a rider moving the pin, a rider changing the address in chat, and a terminal change from T1 to T3 all re-baseline the trip, and the deviation test is re-run against the optimal route between the AMENDED endpoints. That figure is a stored field, not something the tribunal re-derives: amended_optimal_distance_km 24.60 km with amended_optimal_duration_min 31.0. The 21.0 km figure in the claim, rider, is the optimum between Rivervale Drive and Terminal 1 — an itinerary that was never driven once the pin and the terminal changed. The driver is right on that point, and POL-RD-05 also provides that distance driven before each amendment timestamp is not counted against him.\n\nMeasured against the correct baseline, the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00108) records 26.17 km, and POL-RD-01 requires the trace figure rather than the rounded 26.2 km printed on the trip record. The excess is therefore 26.17 − 24.60 = 1.57 km, which is 6.4% of the amended optimal. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is BOTH greater than 20% of the optimal distance AND greater than 0.8 km; the 20% test fails by a wide margin (6.4% against 20%), and both must pass. The rider's POL-RD-01 claim built on the 5.17 km / 24.62% default block is rejected because that block measures against the superseded booked optimum of 21.0 km, which POL-RD-05 forbids. The rider's POL-RD-02 refund computation (6.14, rounded to a payable 6.15) is likewise rejected: POL-RD-02 runs only once a deviation is established, and none is on the amended baseline.\n\nThe rider's point that the driver circled the Terminal 3 kerb for a few minutes is noted but does not change the outcome. Even taking the circling at its highest, the total excess over the amended route is only 1.57 km, already below the threshold; and POL-RD-05 excludes circling within 400 m of an amended dropoff point, which would only reduce the figure. POL-RD-03 and POL-RD-13 are not engaged: no traffic advisory was on file (EV-ADVIS-00108-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0), but neither party asserted an external traffic cause, so there is no traffic excuse to test or discard.\n\nThe trace is clean — 206 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, max gap 0.0 s — so POL-RD-07 does nothing, and no POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires. The fare raises no billing-integrity issue: tolls/ERP 0.00 with no gantries, waiting-time fee 0.00, and airport surcharge 0.00, correctly, because this trip ENDS at Changi rather than originating there, so no surcharge is chargeable under POL-RD-09(4). The driver's profile shows no repeat-deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 402 completed trips in 90 days), so POL-RD-06 needs no referral.\n\nResult: on the correct amended baseline no deviation is established, and under POL-RD-05 and POL-RD-01 the outcome is NO_ACTION. The charged total of $33.77 stands; no refund issues to the rider and no compensation is payable to the driver. The monetary effect of this ruling is nil and no referral is required. Confidence 0.90."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
